{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fc38d60c42ac0e9b","name":"Carrack-Class Light Cruiser","source":{"id":"source:reference-fc38d60c42ac0e9b","title":"Carrack-Class Light Cruiser","revision":18666,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:31:11Z","sha256":"243ee69cfce12d85948ba8c97c2b1a0852382c59ac429c298bf89fe54a9db9ac","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18666","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Carrack-Class%20Light%20Cruiser&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fc38d60c42ac0e9b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," was designed during the waning years of the Republic as a less expensive alternative to other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},". Because of its speed and agility when compared to other Clone Wars-era ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," was used as a fast-attack escort for larger vessels. The design also saw heavy use as an armed escort for merchant convoys, which were continuously targeted by Separatist forces. A group of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carracks"]}," assisted in the destruction of the Separatist flagship ",{"tag":"i","children":["Invisible Hand"]}," during the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After the introduction of larger and more powerful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", groups of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carracks"]}," were more often utilized as scouts and skirmishers for larger fleet elements. In addition, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," was popularly used as a personal transport for Imperial officers and political dignitaries throughout the rise of the Empire.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," is heavily armed for its size. Given the amount of weaponry that a ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," can bring to bear on a target, it poses a significant threat, even to larger enemy vessels. When employed in small squadrons, ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carracks"]}," can wreak havoc on Starships ten times their size.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One reason that ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," crews are so fond of their vessels is that the ship is a sturdy design that incorporates redundant internal bracing and compartmentalized bulkheads. Crew survivability ratings for destroyed and damaged ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carracks"]}," are some of the highest on record. Because of the internal schematics of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]},", it has no significant internal hangar space. Instead, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]}," is equipped with external racks that can transport up to four ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Carrack"]},"-Class Light Cruiser Statistics (CL 18)"]},"\